      "keyInsight": "Your body is a historic house with six front doors: eyes, ears, nose, tongue, skin, and mind. All day long, visitors knock relentlessly. A bright billboard, a siren wailing, the smell of fresh coffee, or a sudden memory. Most people leave all six doors wide open with nobody standing guard. Strays wander in, knock over antique vases, and start kitchen fires. We blame the visitors for our misery. But the visitors are just passing through. Freedom is stationing a courteous, unflinching guard at every doorway who checks every guest without picking fights.",
